---
// One loan's life from origination to default, and when each approach holds a provision.
// Stage colours match the post's cover image.
const ecl = [
  { width: '45%', color: '#2a9d8f', label: 'Stage 1', text: '12-month ECL' },
  { width: '30%', color: '#e9c46a', label: 'Stage 2', text: 'Lifetime ECL' },
  { width: '25%', color: '#e76f51', label: 'Stage 3', text: 'Lifetime, impaired' },
];
---

<figure class="not-prose my-10">
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-surface p-5 sm:p-6">
    <div>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium">Incurred loss <span class="font-normal text-muted">· today</span></p>
      <div class="mt-2 flex h-11 overflow-hidden rounded-lg text-xs font-medium sm:text-sm">
        <div class="flex w-[75%] items-center border border-dashed border-line px-3 text-muted">No provision yet</div>
        <div class="flex w-[25%] items-center px-3 text-[#0b1f3a]" style="background:#e76f51">Provision</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium">Expected credit loss <span class="font-normal text-muted">· from 2028</span></p>
      <div class="mt-2 flex h-11 overflow-hidden rounded-lg text-xs font-medium text-[#0b1f3a] sm:text-sm">
        {
          ecl.map((s) => (
            <div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col justify-center px-3 leading-tight" style={`width:${s.width};background:${s.color}`}>
              <span class="truncate">{s.label}</span>
              <span class="hidden truncate font-normal opacity-80 sm:block">{s.text}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-3 flex text-xs text-muted" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="w-[45%] border-l border-line pl-2">Loan made</span>
      <span class="w-[30%] border-l border-line pl-2">Credit risk rises</span>
      <span class="w-[25%] border-l border-line pl-2">Default</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center text-sm text-muted">
    The same loan under both approaches. ECL holds a provision from day one and raises it as risk rises.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
